# Numbered calc chains

## Outside a proof

Some text before the chain, long enough to show where the text column starts and ends, so the chain can be compared with it.

$$ {:label: eq-before}
\|F(x)-F(y)\|^2 \ge c_0\sum_{j=1}^{k}a_j^2 .
$$

The bound :ref:eq-before:: gives

:calc: {:label: eq-top}

  :step: $\|F(x)-F(y)\|^2 \ \ge\ c_0\sum_{j=1}^{k}a_j^2$

    :p: Because the first reason holds. ::

  ::

  :step: $\ge\ \frac{c_0}{k}\Big(\sum_{j=1}^{k}a_j\Big)^2$

    :p: Because $\sum_{j=1}^{k} a_j \le k$. ::

  ::

  :step: $\ge\ \frac{c_0}{4L}\,d(x,y)^2 .$

    :p: Because the third reason holds. ::

  ::

::

Text after the chain. By :ref:eq-top::, the bound holds.

## Inside a proof

:theorem: {
  :label: thm-calc-num
  :title: A bound proved by a numbered calculation
}

  The bound holds.

::

:proof: {:of: thm-calc-num}

  :step: A preliminary step. ::

  :step: {:label: stp-calc-num-host}

    :claim: The calculation below establishes the bound. ::

    :p:

      :calc: {:label: eq-inproof}

        :step: $f(x) = a - b$

          :p: Because the first reason holds. ::

        ::

        :step: $\le \sum_{j=1}^{k} c_j$

          :p: Because the second reason holds. ::

        ::

      ::

    :: ::

::

By :ref:eq-inproof::, done.
